Z||000002||BAM-BAM||04-21-2001||10:51 PM||||  I feel what you're sayin. It seems that the world is fading fast. Laden with coruption, greed and a general lack of basic human compassion. Everyone wants theirs and they don't care who they have to hurt to get it. Just look at the corporate world and you'll see what I mean. Use them for what you can get out of them, then cast them to the wolves. When people are treated as such, their mentalities change, anger and hate become the driving forces in their lives, bent on retribution. Individualy people in general are wanting more and giving less. I work with bight and talented people and I watch them squander their talents and abilities just to take longer breaks, lunches and just plain not work. But when payday comes along, they demand theirs. It's a sick world and I can't see a way to change it other than starting at the top. Start with the Federal, State and local governments, move on down to the corporations and so on to the individuals themselves. Get everyone thinking about giving what they get and getting what they give. Begain making people responsible for their actions instead of excusing them based on some discrete technicality. The 1st amendment to the constitution has been completely perverted to alow anyone to speak out agains what is morally correct yet in the same breath condem morality as faciast. I don't know man, When children can divorce their parents and children can be prosecuted as adults, and Homosexuality and lesbianism are correct and heterosexuality is prudish, I think we need to rethink some things. Listen to modern music, Rap, I like it all, but I'm an adult. The problem here is that children are the target audience. Hell, they hardly even bleep out the harsh stuff anymore. No one wants to be responsible for their influences on the world, but they want the world to teat them fairly. Can't explain it man, it's the Lawyers, they bend and tweek and prostitute the constitution, federal and local laws to get what they are hired to get. In the end, they establish laws and precidence that govern our everyday lives. Enough for now, I'm getting a headache. I would enjoy more chatting about all this again.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||12
Z||000003||Cameron||04-21-2001||11:09 PM||||bam-bam I like your signature ... unfortunately that isn't entirely true.  I mean think about it.  We have people that can become some of the most influential people in the country and be entirely stupid.  Take a quick look at bill gates not to name names or anything.  Personally, I think that he is a good business man, but he has really crappy morals to say the least.  He lied, cheated and stole to get where he is right now.  Yet people all of the world look up to him.  It's not brains that win anymore its the lieing, cheating and stealing.  Unfortunately, I would consider myself an honest person, well unless you include my past and my parents. :blink:<P>But it is really starting to make me sick.  I just got turned down for a job offer, because I was too young.  What the heck is this.  It was a government job and you have to be old enough to have gone through college, even if you havn't.  That is a crock if I have ever heard one.  I would think that I am old enough to work.  I'm 18 for Pete's sake ( not to upset anybody ).  And you know the funny part about it all.  And most likely a guy with less experience is going to get hired and not be able to get the job done.  I had more experience then they wanted and I wanted less money then they were offering.  And it is all because I wasn't honest when I told my recruiter my age.  If I would have lied I would have gotten the job.<P>Life sucks.  Well, I guess that's not entirely true.  Life is ok, but some of the people you have to live it with suck.<P>Well, I guess I have talked enough right now.  I gotta go workout, see if I can calm down.<P>------------------<BR>Cameron<BR> <A HREF="http://Fiero.NetMARC.com" TARGET=_blank>http://Fiero.NetMARC.com</A> ||||reg||9
Z||000004||2xsess||04-21-2001||11:22 PM||||Dang BAM, you said it all, but Cameron is right, sometimes the lying and all that other stuff get the wrong people in powerful positions. Sad state of affairs if you ask me. I have decided that I feel sorry for all the children of today and the future, I fear what type of evironment they'll grow up in.<P>A recent trip back to my hometown in PA showed me just how truly horrible things can get. Simple manners have been forgotten, almost if everyone is too busy or rushed to take the time to say "excuse me"in order to get passed you or when they bump into you. Some people may think such things are trivial but why should treating your fellow man with a little respect be trivial?!? As much as I dislike the heat and general climate of the south, I now truly appreciate the "Southern Hospitality"<P>Sorry, had to find a place to vent and Galen left an opening  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>  <B>*For Sale*<BR>        $2000obo</B>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">        <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT Bastard||04-21-2001||11:41 PM||||I hear what you're all saying.  There are many times when I feel like people are well-beyond repair.  There's times when it's bad enough that I could care less whether I'm alive or dead.   Not that I would kill myself... Even if I knew my life would end like a Greek tragedy, I owe it to myself to see how it ends.   I've stopped watching news/tv and I feel slightly better being ignorant to the world.  When I hear someone listening to stuff news(Rush Limbaugh) I get annoyed because I hate the senseless bickering and bad news.   I want to be ALIVE while I'm alive, not drown in the filth of society.  I'm only 20, and in the past 2 years that I've lived on my own I've learned so much.  I basically decided that I'll focus on the things that DO make me happy(not sick) and build my life around them.  I choose my friends VERY carefully, and try to be mellow all-around.  I try to be kind where others fail to do so.  I live for the thrills that I get from racing.  In this world we are surrounded by weeds.  It's our job to find the flowers amidst them, no matter how scarce they are.   I still live out a majority of my day being depressed over the hopelessness of the human race and my lack of faith in it(endless examples.)  But even one good thing a day can turn it all around(ex: talking with an old friend, etc...)  I guess my most recent outlook on life is stated in this quote from some famous guy:  "The ball is round, the game lasts 90 minutes.  These are facts.  All the rest is pure theory."  We know that we live and die, and that's IT!  Nobody knows how we should live, and we probably never will. This is an admittedly godless philiosophy, but that's an argument for another day. Thankyou and goodbye.<P>-Captain McJeff||||reg||1
Z||000006||RobertVol||04-22-2001||12:20 AM||||Generally I agree with the lack of compassion in the World today. And for the most part you guys are right. Our society has been trained or our hearts have been hardened because of how our society promotes violence and the media makes things like school shootings look like a sweeps week. <P>But just when I think everyone is going to hell in a handbasket I run into someone nice or that has compassion and think well there are few left in the world. You dont have to look any further than this Forum to prove it! <P>And being in the South I do appreciate Suthern hospitality   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>And .........<P>Thats all I Got ta Suy 'Bout that!<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Rob ..............................OUT!<P>[This message has been edited by RobertVol (edited 04-22-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by RobertVol (edited 04-22-2001).]||||reg||14
