Z||000008||Tryxalon||04-22-2001||11:00 AM||||Now guys, don't get me wrong, I'm not trying to downplay your angst, to belittle your feelings of insecurity, to invalidate your world view. <P><BR><B>HOWEVER </B> [u]my[/u] perceptions are a little different, perhaps because of extensive travel for many years in OTHER countries and a life-long study of history.<P>I am in the USA. I feel that with our system of government and society this is the greatest place in the world! With the current world situation (the total, neccesarily local conditions may be temporarily "excrement laden" example: Gabon and Liberia) today is the best that local and global economy, health, scientific advance, and opportunity <B> have ever been!!! </B>  <P>Point is: I get enough of doom and gloom "Chicken Little - ism" by "Luddite eco-nuts", rightwing conspiracy theorists, "give me your money" socialists, and "Have I got a deal to fleece you" capitalists on other boards. <P>Here: I got a hell of a great little car that gives me a woody everytime I drive it!!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Galen||04-22-2001||03:02 PM||||Man, we didn't need to know that. heh<P>but seriously, maybe this is a great country.. maybe it is, I'm not condeming the goverment, I wont, I think they are all full of sh!t yes... but they do their job, even if it is not always the greatest. <P>This country is fuxxed up cuz of the media. And activist groups, people ever heard of freedom of choice? Its my choice to dow hat I wanna do, as long as its within the laws. The goverment is full of sh!t, as are most of the population. Remember, before they became politicians, they were the public.<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Spektyr||04-22-2001||03:42 PM||||Well, thanks to our government (the military specifically) I have a 'broken' feature in my psyche... highly variable moral code.<P>Switched on, I can sympathize.  Switched off, I'm one of the jerks.  The big problem is it's a lot easier to turn it off than on.  "Morals Optional" is the term I use.  A useful feature if your job requires you to do things that a sane person can't cope with, but generally more trouble than it's worth since pretty much anyone that meets you with them switched off isn't ever going to like you.<P>But like a badly worn gear shift you end up with a less positive lock on what gear your mind is in, and most of the time I operate in the "Do unto others as they do unto you" mode.  If you're nice to me, I'm the nicest guy in the world.  If you play by the 'naughty' rules... well I'm trained to be a pain in the rear.  So I'm not amoral, just not entirely moral either.<P>If Social Entropy is the way things are going... well I can try to make things better and maybe get plowed over by the Bill Gates of the world, or maybe I play by their rules when I take the field against them.  Sometimes it seems that taking the moral high ground doesn't do much but make you the target of choice when everyone else is in their foxholes.<P>Right?  Wrong?  I don't know.  Maybe there never really was such a thing.  I just try to be as nice as I can without wandering into a pack of wolves with a porkchop tied around my neck.  I mean the wolves would think that was nice of me, right?<P>Maybe the people like me are doing a good thing, doing bad things to the ones doing evil to the nice people.  Because the people that are truely the "Good People" can't really do the bad stuff without breaking a part of who they are.<P>Maybe it's just a lame excuse to not force the gearshift all the way to "Moral" and then welding it in place.<P>I don't know, I only see grey anymore.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
