Z||000020||fyerstarter||04-26-2001||11:32 AM||||Black 88: Your prob right about WW1, I didn't reference my history books when writing this but the point is that every era has it's good and it's bad times, and the grass is always greener on the other side. When my generation gets old we'll probably be sitting in our rocking chairs grumbling about how life was so much better in the 1990's, but it's not going to be true is it?<P>Galen: What Im saying is, <P>"Quit your bitchin! Life is good. It has never been better"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by fyerstarter (edited 04-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||Fiero5||04-26-2001||12:37 PM||||Well, if I let my Fiero(s) get me down everytime they have a problem or needed some stupid repair, I would have been a mental case a year ago.<P>We have 12 Fieros all running. Every week one out of this groupe needs something. I could go on for about 4 pages about what we have experienced in the last month alone. For example: My 86 SS trashed the timing gear on the way home from CT and it cost me over hundred bucks to get it towed the rest of the way home at midnight. My Dad has spent a week trying to replace the gear and get the stupid seal NOT to leak at all. After going thru two of the seals, it is still giving my dad problems so he is building a handmade mech to help set up the seal correctly. The same time this is going on, my sons 85GT blew a tranny line. On the way home trying to just get it home he is followed by a local cop who pulls him over as his police car is getting sprayed with tranny fluid. My son had to leave it at that spot and the cop gave him a fix it ticket and ride to our place. This was at 11pm. I went back and got the car after puting in some tranny fluid. When he took it in for repair, they didn't do a good job the first time so he had to waste time and take it back. For the inconvenience they did the tranny line on the other side for free. Can you say Bonus? Then Marians 84 rod knock get's worse and we have to put it up. During all this, Fiero 8 starts...well, I think you get the idea? This is just in the last three weeks actually.<P>So..if I get upset and sad, it won't change anything. These things will still happen. We just handle them one at a time. Well, maybe two at a time on accassion  Heh, heh, heh<P>Cheer up dude.<P>Your fellow Fiero friend, <P>Steve||||reg||10
